ckly Dale any closing thoughts  for the audience any closing thoughts I  just thought of one other thing is is  there in terms of a show it has anybody  here use spanner or big table can we we  don't have a ton of people but I mean  interestingly enough I think it's  Spotify that put out a open-source tool  for actually scaling up and down  BigTable and and we actually modified  that to work for spanner and that made a  significant difference so I don't know I  think making cause a cause public in  looking for these kind of things cuz  auto scaling is like one of the things  that really does reduce cost I mean it's  the promise of the cloud right so my  thoughts make your cost visible and and  I guess just look at always working on  it maybe one order slowly tactical thing  that we haven't talked on we didn't  really talk too much about networking  it'd be worthwhile to look at how much  your data is spanning within a zone but  also between zones and across regions  some of that might be unintentional you  might be charging a little bit more than  you expect to there and may not be  getting a benefit so just looking at  where your job you're there's traveling  across the zones and regions could be  worthwhile yeah I I would like to read  at one point of understanding the  importance of cost management solution  in place so if you're not already  thinking about it that I would want to  reiterate and another thing in terms of  we talked about how do you we talked  about tooling in many organizations you  don't have a choice of coming up with  for example data story we looked at at  many customers but many organizations  already have a tooling for cost  management because DCP is not their  first cost component they may have other  closed private cloud Colo all other  things so you may not have a choice in  terms of tooling but make that choice  early on because one example one  experience we had was in one of the  retailers we started off with the  on-prem data storage